.TH INTENT 1 "2026-10-26" "intent 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
intent \- keyboard-first, local-first task management
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B intent
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B intent
is a keyboard-first, local-first task manager built around a Vim-like command
grammar. Tasks live in a single SQLite database; the CLI and the GPUI desktop
application (\fBintent-gui\fR, see \fBintent-gui(1)\fR) share one database and
may run concurrently.
.PP
Pass
.B \-\-json
to any command for machine-readable output: one JSON value on stdout, and on
error a single JSON object on stderr of the form
.B {"error":{"code":...,"message":...}}.
Error codes are stable:
.BR not_found ", " bad_date ", " bad_value ", " usage ", " io ", " db .
.SS Task model
Tasks have a stable 6-character
.IR id ", a single-line " title ", multi-line " notes ", a lifecycle " status
.RB ( active ", " done ", " archived "),
an inbox flag, a priority (none|low|medium|high), an optional free-form
project, tags, and three optional dates: \fBdue\fR (hard deadline),
\fBremind\fR (soft resurfacing), and \fBdefer_until\fR (hidden from Today
until then).
.PP
Capturing requires no metadata; captured tasks land in the inbox. A task
leaves the inbox when it gains a project, a due date, a remind date, or an
explicit organize. Priority, tags, notes, and title edits never clear the
inbox.
.SS Views
.TP
.B inbox
captured, not yet organized (newest first)
.TP
.B today
active tasks due or reminding today, not deferred (due date ascending, then
priority, then oldest)
.TP
.B upcoming
active, organized, not in today (soonest first, undated "someday" last)
.TP
.B completed
status done (newest first)
.TP
.B archived
status archived (newest first)
.TP
.B all
everything except archived (default for \fBlist\fR)
.SS Dates
Everywhere a date is accepted:
.BR YYYY-MM-DD ", " today ", " tod ", " tomorrow ", " tom ", " tmr ", "
.BR yesterday ", " +N "[d|w|m|y], " \-N [d|w|m|y], a weekday name
.RB ( mon .. sun ,
next occurrence, today included), and
.B none
or
.B \-
where clearing is allowed.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "intent add " TITLE
Capture a new task (alias for the title:
.BR \-\-title ).
Options:
.BR \-\-notes ,
.B \-\-due ,
.B \-\-remind ,
.B \-\-priority ,
.BR \-\-project ,
.BR \-\-tags " a,b," 
.B \-\-no\-inbox .
Assigning
.BR \-\-project ,
.B \-\-due ,
or
.B \-\-remind
implies leaving the inbox.
.TP
.BI "intent list [" VIEW "]"
List a view (inbox|today|upcoming|completed|archived|all; default all).
Filters:
.BR \-\-project ", " \-\-tag ", " \-\-priority ", " \-\-query ", " \-\-limit .
.TP
.BI "intent show " ID
Show one task in full.
.TP
.BI "intent edit " ID
Edit fields; at least one flag required:
.BR \-\-title ", " \-\-notes ", " \-\-due ", " \-\-remind ", " \-\-defer\-until ,
.BR \-\-priority ", " \-\-project ", " \-\-tags ", " \-\-tag\-add ", " \-\-tag\-rm .
Dates and projects accept
.B none
/
.B \-
to clear.
.TP
.BI "intent done " ID
Complete a task.
.TP
.BI "intent reopen " ID
Reopen a completed task.
.TP
.BI "intent defer " "ID DATE"
Hide from Today until DATE (or
.B none
to clear).
.TP
.BI "intent prioritize " "ID LEVEL"
Set priority: none|low|medium|high (aliases \-/l/m/h).
.TP
.BI "intent archive " ID
Move out of sight (reversible with
.BR unarchive ).
.TP
.BI "intent unarchive " ID
Bring an archived task back to active.
.TP
.BI "intent organize " "ID [\-\-project P]"
Take a task out of the inbox, optionally assigning a project.
.TP
.BI "intent delete " ID
Permanently delete. Asks y/N on a TTY; refuses without
.B \-\-force
in non-interactive mode.
.TP
.BI "intent search " QUERY
ANDed case-insensitive terms over title/notes/project/tags; archived excluded.
.TP
.B intent counts
Per-view task counts.
.TP
.BI "intent completions " SHELL
Print a completion script for
.BR bash ", " zsh ", or " fish
on stdout. Does not access the database.
.TP
.B intent help [COMMAND]
Show help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
success
.TP
.B 1
runtime error (database, io)
.TP
.B 2
usage error (bad flags)
.TP
.B 3
task not found
.TP
.B 4
invalid value (date, priority, ...)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B INTENT_DB
Path to the SQLite database file. When unset or empty, the default path is
used instead.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base for the default database path
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/intent/tasks.db ;
falls back to
.IR ~/.local/share/intent/tasks.db 
.SH FILES
.I ~/.local/share/intent/tasks.db
(default database; WAL mode)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR intent-gui (1)
